invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_avx2.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: rsa_avx2.c drops the target attribute that turns AVX2 on for its
  own functions, so the kernel compiles only where the whole object is
  built with AVX2, and an object built that way runs AVX2 in code the
  caller's CH_CPU_AVX2 bit never chose. The script compiles the file for
  x86-64 with no instruction flag, as a host object compiles it, and the
  compile fails: each intrinsic needs a feature that only the attribute
  turned on.

--- old
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("avx2"))), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#pragma GCC target("avx2")
#endif

#include "rsa_avx2_lanes.h"
--- new
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((cold)), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#endif

#include "rsa_avx2_lanes.h"
